d release 5.2. <b>So-what:</b> almost certainly caused by the release, not by users or competitors.</p>"},{"q":"What would you check next?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li>Crash rate and app-start success on 5.2</li> <li><b>Push notification delivery</b>: lesson reminders bring back many users; a change in permissions could silently stop them</li> <li>Funnel: open app → start lesson → finish lesson, to see where Android users drop</li></ul> <p><i>Interviewer reveals:</i> reminder notifications delivered on Android fell from 92% to 15% after 5.2, because a new permission prompt is declined by most users.</p>"},{"q":"What do you do now?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li><b>Now:</b> hotfix that asks for the permission at a better moment, with a clear explanation (e.g. after the user's first lesson streak)</li> <li><b>Recover:</b> email/in-app message to affected users to switch reminders back on</li> <li><b>Prevent:</b> add 'notifications delivered' to release checklists and alerts</li></ul>"}],"reco":"The 8% drop is an Android problem caused by release 5.2: a new notification permission is being declined, so reminders no longer reach most users and fewer come back for lessons. Ship a hotfix that asks for the permission at a better moment, win back affected users by email, and add notification delivery to the release checklist so it can't happen silently again.","great":["Checks data and definitions first","Segments before guessing","Confirms the size (45% × 18% ≈ 8%)","Fixes now and prevents it happening again"],"id":15,"slug":"lingualeap"}